	('9edb8d9b-9c39-4de2-a019-b32a143f05c5', '"{\"demographics\":{\"DOBDay\":\"11\",\"DOBMonth\":\"April\",\"admissionDateOffest\":\"1\",\"admissionTime\":\"14:42\",\"admittingDiagnosis\":\"Acute GI Bleed with Symptomatic Anemia\",\"age\":\"68\",\"attendingProviderName\":\"Alex Reynolds,,\",\"attendingProviderTitle\":\"MD\",\"codeStatus\":\"Full\",\"dosingWeight\":\"86\",\"employment\":\"Construction Work\",\"firstName\":\"Thomas\",\"heightFeet\":\"6\",\"heightInches\":\"1\",\"insurance\":\"Private\",\"language\":\"Englsih\",\"needsInterpreter\":false,\"lastName\":\"Dunn\",\"precautions\":\"\",\"relationshipStatus\":\"Widowed\",\"religion\":\"Lutheran\",\"summary\":\"68-year-old male presents with progressive fatigue, dizziness, and dark tarry stools for 3 days. Reports worsening weakness with near-syncope when standing. Mild epigastric discomfort. Denies vomiting blood. Denies chest pain.\",\"contact\":\"William Dunn\",\"contactRelationship\":\"Brother\",\"contactPhone\":\"(616) 237-8944\"},\"history\":{\"medicalHistory\":[\"HTN\",\"Type 2 DM\",\"Atrial fibrillation\",\"Stage 3 CKD\",\"Peptic ulcer disease\"],\"surgicalHistory\":[],\"allergies\":[\"Sulfa\",\"Morphine\"],\"socialHistory\":[\"2-3 drinks/day\",\"Former smoker- quit 2 years ago\"],\"livingSituation\":[\"Lives alone\"],\"alerts\":[\"High Risk for Falls - Morse score > 45\",\"Pressure Injury Risk (Braden <18)\",\"Anticoagulant Therapy - Bleeding Precautions\",\"NPO Status\"],\"familyHistory\":[{\"relation\":\"Father\",\"condition\":\"Deceased, heart attack\"},{\"relation\":\"Mother\",\"condition\":\"Type 2 DM\"},{\"relation\":\"Brother\",\"condition\":\"HTN\"}]},\"notes\":[{\"title\":\"History & Physical Note\",\"author\":\"Dr. Regan Vanderwood\",\"specialty\":\"Emergency Medicine\",\"timeOffset\":-2160,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p><strong>History of Present Illness</strong></p><p>68-year-old male presents with progressive fatigue, dizziness, and dark tarry stools for 3 days. Reports worsening weakness today with near-syncope when standing. Mild epigastric discomfort. Denies vomiting blood. Denies chest pain.</p><p>States he takes apixaban for atrial fibrillation.</p><p>Concern for acute GI bleed with symptomatic anemia.</p><p><strong>Past Medical History</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>HTN</p></li><li><p>Type 2 DM</p></li><li><p>Atrial fibrillation</p></li><li><p>Peptic ulcer disease</p></li><li><p>Stage 3 CKD</p></li></ul><p><strong>Home Medications</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Lisinopril 10 mg daily</p></li><li><p>Metformin 1000 mg BID</p></li><li><p>Apixaban (Eliquis) 5 mg BID</p></li><li><p>Pantoprazole 40 mg daily</p></li><li><p>Ferrous sulfate</p></li></ul><p><strong>Review of Systems</strong></p><p>Positive:</p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Fatigue</p></li><li><p>Dizziness</p></li><li><p>Melena</p></li><li><p>Weakness</p></li></ul><p>Negative:</p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Hematemesis</p></li><li><p>Chest pain</p></li><li><p>SOB</p></li><li><p>Fever</p></li><li><p>Trauma</p></li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Physical Exam</strong></p><p><strong>General: </strong>Pale, fatigued appearing, slow to sit upright</p><p><strong>Cardiac: </strong>Tachycardic, irregular rhythm</p><p><strong>Respiratory: </strong>Clear bilaterally</p><p><strong>Abdomen: </strong>Soft, mild epigastric tenderness, no rebound</p><p><strong>Rectal: </strong>Black tarry stool, guaiac positive</p><p><strong>Skin: </strong>Cool, pale</p><p><strong>Neuro: </strong>Alert and oriented x4</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>ED Labs (Initial)</strong></p><p>Hgb 9.4, Hct 29, WBC 8.4, Plt 240, BUN 28, Cr 1.3, INR 1.6, K 3.6</p><p><strong>Imaging</strong></p><p>CT Abdomen/Pelvis: No perforation. Possible upper GI source</p><p><strong>ED Management</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>2 large-bore IVs placed</p></li><li><p>1L NS bolus</p></li><li><p>IV pantoprazole bolus + infusion</p></li><li><p>Type &amp; screen sent</p></li><li><p>Held apixaban</p></li><li><p>Serial CBCs ordered</p></li><li><p>GI consult requested</p></li></ul><p><strong>Medical Decision Making</strong></p><p>Presentation consistent with likely upper GI bleed given melena and elevated BUN. Occult stool positive. Hemodynamically borderline. At risk for further decline and anemia. Will admit to med-surg for monitoring, serial labs, and possible transfusion.</p>\"},{\"title\":\"Nursing Note\",\"author\":\"Tessa Ludwig, RN\",\"specialty\":\"Nursing\",\"timeOffset\":-2040,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p><strong>Chief Complaint:</strong><br>“I feel really weak and dizzy… and my stools have been black.”</p><p><strong>Initial Vitals</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Temp: 98.2°F (36.8°C)</p></li><li><p>HR: 104</p></li><li><p>BP: 102/64</p></li><li><p>RR: 18</p></li><li><p>SpO₂: 98% RA</p></li><li><p>Pain: 3/10 epigastric discomfort</p></li></ul><p><strong>Triage Assessment</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Pale appearance</p></li><li><p>Slow gait</p></li><li><p>Reports fatigue x 3–4 days</p></li><li><p>2 episodes near-syncope today</p></li><li><p>Black, tarry stools x 2 days</p></li><li><p>Denies hematemesis</p></li><li><p>On anticoagulant (Eliquis)</p></li></ul><p></p>\"},{\"title\":\"Nursing Note\",\"author\":\"Sierra Johnson, RN\",\"specialty\":\"Nursing\",\"timeOffset\":-1920,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p>Patient admitted to inpatient unit. Continues to report weakness and lightheadedness. Skin pale and cool. IV fluids infusing. No active vomiting. Education provided on NPO status and fall precautions.</p>\"},{\"title\":\"Progress Note\",\"author\":\"Alex Reynolds, MD\",\"specialty\":\"Internal Medicine\",\"timeOffset\":-1680,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p><strong>Subjective: </strong>Patient reports ongoing fatigue and intermittent dizziness. Denies hematemesis but continues to have black stools. Mild epigastric discomfort persists. No chest pain or shortness of breath.</p><p><strong>Objective:</strong></p><p>Vital Signs:</p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Temp: 98.4°F</p></li><li><p>HR: 102</p></li><li><p>BP: 100/62</p></li><li><p>RR: 18</p></li><li><p>SpO₂: 98% RA</p></li></ul><p><strong>Physical Exam:</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>General: Pale, fatigued</p></li><li><p>Cardiac: Irregularly irregular rhythm</p></li><li><p>Abdomen: Mild epigastric tenderness, no guarding</p></li><li><p>Skin: Cool, pale</p></li><li><p>Neuro: A&amp;O x4</p></li></ul><p><strong>Labs Reviewed</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Hgb: 8.6 → trending downward</p></li><li><p>BUN elevated (suggestive of GI bleed)</p></li><li><p>INR mildly elevated (on anticoagulant)</p></li></ul><p><strong>Assessment</strong></p><ol class=\\\"list-decimal ml-10\\\" type=\\\"1\\\"><li><p>Suspected upper GI bleed</p></li><li><p>Symptomatic anemia (developing)</p></li><li><p>Atrial fibrillation on anticoagulation</p></li><li><p>CKD stage 3</p></li></ol><p><strong>Plan</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Serial CBC q8h</p></li><li><p>Continue IV pantoprazole infusion</p></li><li><p>Hold apixaban</p></li><li><p>IV fluids</p></li><li><p>GI consult for EGD</p></li><li><p>Monitor for signs of hemodynamic instability</p></li><li><p>Fall precautions</p></li></ul><p></p>\"},{\"title\":\"Consult Note\",\"author\":\"Amir Patel, MD\",\"specialty\":\"Gastroenterology\",\"timeOffset\":-1560,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p><strong>Reason for Consult: </strong>Melena and suspected upper GI bleed</p><p><strong>HPI: </strong>68-year-old male with history of peptic ulcer disease and anticoagulation presents with melena and symptomatic anemia. Progressive fatigue and orthostatic symptoms.</p><p><strong>Assessment</strong></p><p>High suspicion for <strong>upper GI bleed</strong>, likely:</p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Peptic ulcer disease (most likely)</p></li><li><p>Possible anticoagulation-related bleeding</p></li></ul><p><strong>Plan</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Urgent EGD within 24 hours</p></li><li><p>Continue IV pantoprazole infusion</p></li><li><p>Hold anticoagulants</p></li><li><p>Maintain hemodynamic stability</p></li><li><p>Transfuse PRN</p></li><li><p>NPO</p></li></ul><p></p>\"},{\"title\":\"Nursing Note\",\"author\":\"Sierra Johnson, RN\",\"specialty\":\"Nursing\",\"timeOffset\":-1440,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p>Patient reports weakness and shortness of breath. Dark stool x2. Lightheaded with ambulation.</p>\"},{\"title\":\"Progress Note\",\"author\":\"Alex Reynolds, MD\",\"specialty\":\"Internal Medicine\",\"timeOffset\":-1200,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p><strong>Subjective:</strong> Patient reports worsening weakness and dizziness. States he feels “lightheaded when standing.” Reports continued dark stools overnight.</p><p><strong>Objective:</strong></p><p>Vital Signs:</p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>HR: 110</p></li><li><p>BP: 94/58</p></li><li><p>RR: 20</p></li></ul><p><strong>Physical Exam:</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Increased pallor</p></li><li><p>Orthostatic hypotension present</p></li><li><p>Abdomen unchanged</p></li></ul><p><strong>Labs</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Hgb: 8.6 → 7.4</p></li><li><p>BUN rising</p></li><li><p>K decreasing</p></li></ul><p><strong>Assessment</strong></p><ol class=\\\"list-decimal ml-10\\\" type=\\\"1\\\"><li><p>Active upper GI bleed – ongoing blood loss</p></li><li><p>Worsening anemia</p></li><li><p>Volume depletion</p></li><li><p>Electrolyte imbalance (hypokalemia)</p></li></ol><p><strong>Plan</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Continue IV PPI infusion</p></li><li><p>Replace potassium</p></li><li><p>Maintain IV fluids</p></li><li><p>Type &amp; crossmatch</p></li><li><p>Prepare for EGD today</p></li><li><p>Anticipate need for transfusion if Hgb &lt;7 or symptomatic- blood consent obtained and in patient chart</p></li></ul><p></p>\"},{\"title\":\"Post-op Note\",\"author\":\"Amir Patel, MD\",\"specialty\":\"Gastroenterology\",\"timeOffset\":-960,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p><strong>Esophagogastroduodenoscopy (EGD)</strong><br><strong>Endoscopist:</strong> Amir Patel, MD</p><p><strong>Indication: </strong>Melena and symptomatic anemia</p><p><strong>Findings</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p><strong>Actively bleeding gastric ulcer</strong> (lesser curvature)</p></li><li><p>Visible vessel present</p></li><li><p>No esophageal varices</p></li><li><p>No perforation</p></li></ul><p><strong>Interventions Performed</strong></p><ol class=\\\"list-decimal ml-10\\\" type=\\\"1\\\"><li><p>Epinephrine Injection</p></li></ol><p>o Injected into and around ulcer base</p><p>o Purpose: vasoconstriction to reduce bleeding</p><ol class=\\\"list-decimal ml-10\\\" start=\\\"2\\\" type=\\\"1\\\"><li><p>Thermal Coagulation (Cautery)</p></li></ol><p>o Applied to bleeding vessel</p><p>o Purpose: achieve hemostasis</p><ol class=\\\"list-decimal ml-10\\\" start=\\\"3\\\" type=\\\"1\\\"><li><p>Hemostatic Clip Placement</p></li></ol><p>o Clip placed over visible vessel</p><p>o Purpose: mechanically stop bleeding</p><p><strong>Outcome</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Bleeding controlled</p></li><li><p>No immediate complications</p></li><li><p>Patient tolerated procedure well</p></li></ul><p><strong>Post-Procedure Orders</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Continue IV PPI infusion (72 hrs)</p></li><li><p>NPO initially → advance diet</p></li><li><p>Monitor for re-bleeding:</p></li></ul><p>o melena</p><p>o hematemesis</p><p>o dropping Hgb</p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Serial CBCs</p></li></ul><p>Avoid NSAIDs/anticoagulants</p>\"},{\"title\":\"Progress Note\",\"author\":\"Amir Patel, MD\",\"specialty\":\"Gastroenterology\",\"timeOffset\":-720,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p>Patient underwent EGD. Bleeding gastric ulcer identified and treated.</p><p><strong>Assessment Update</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Source of bleed confirmed: <strong>gastric ulcer</strong></p></li><li><p>Hemostasis achieved endoscopically</p></li><li><p>Still high risk for re-bleed</p></li></ul><p><strong>Plan</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Continue PPI infusion x 72 hours</p></li><li><p>NPO → advance diet per GI</p></li><li><p>Monitor Hgb closely- 7.2</p></li><li><p>Transfuse PRBCs if symptomatic or Hgb &lt;7</p></li><li><p>Continue telemetry</p></li><li><p>Colonoscopy planned for full evaluation</p></li></ul><p></p>\"},{\"title\":\"Progress Note\",\"author\":\"Alex Reynolds, MR\",\"specialty\":\"Internal Medicine\",\"timeOffset\":-240,\"excludedFromPresim\":false,\"content\":\"<p><strong>Assessment:</strong><br>68 y/o male with upper GI bleed secondary to gastric ulcer. Progressive symptomatic anemia. Orthostatic and tachycardic. Hgb 6.9.</p><p><strong>Plan:</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Transfuse 2 units PRBCs</p></li><li><p>Monitor closely for transfusion reaction</p></li><li><p>Continue IV pantoprazole infusion</p></li><li><p>Hold anticoagulation</p></li><li><p>Colonoscopy tomorrow</p></li><li><p>Maintain K &gt; 3.5</p></li><li><p>Strict I&amp;O</p></li></ul><p></p>\"}],\"orders\":[{\"category\":\"Laboratory\",\"title\":\"Basic Metabolic Panel (BMP)\",\"details\":\"Collect Basic Metabolic Panel (BMP).\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Respiratory\",\"title\":\"Oxygen Therapy\",\"details\":\"Administer oxygen via nasal cannula at 2 L/min. Titrate to maintain SpO₂ ≥ 92%.\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Azzedine Habz\",\"important\":false,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Vital Signs Monitoring (q4h)\",\"details\":\"Monitor BP, HR, RR, Temp, SpO₂ every 4 hours. Notify provider for Temp > 38.0°C (100.4°F), Systolic BP > 160 mmHg or < 100 mmHg, HR > 110 bpm or < 50 bpm.\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Insert and Maintain IV\",\"details\":\"\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Blood Glucose Monitoring (ACHS)\",\"details\":\"Monitor blood glucose before meals and at bedtime (ACHS). Notify provider for blood glucose < 70 mg/dL or > 300 mg/dL.\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Activity: As Tolerated\",\"details\":\"Encourage patient activity as tolerated. Assist with ambulation as needed.\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"important\":false,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Fall Risk Precautions\",\"details\":\"Implement standard fall risk protocol. Ensure bed in low position and call light within reach.\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"important\":false,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Diet\",\"title\":\"NPO\",\"details\":\"NPO except medications\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Vanderwood\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"PRBC\",\"details\":\"Prepare and Transfuse 2 units PRBC. Monitor for signs of transfusion reaction.\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Reynolds\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":false},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Telemetry\",\"details\":\"Continuous cardiac monitoring- symptomatic anemia/acute electrolyte imbalance\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Vanderwood\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Laboratory\",\"title\":\"Complete Blood Count (CBC)\",\"details\":\"Q8 hours- notify provider if Hgb <7.0\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Vanderwood\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true}],\"labs\":{\"data\":[{\"field\":\"Metabolic\",\"rowType\":\"divider\",\"unit\":\"\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Sodium\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(mEq/L)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":135,\"high\":145},\"-2160\":\"138\",\"-1680\":\"137\",\"-1200\":\"135\",\"-720\":\"134\",\"-240\":\"134\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Potassium\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(mEq/L)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":3.5,\"high\":5},\"criticalRange\":{\"low\":3,\"high\":6},\"-2160\":\"3.6\",\"-1680\":\"3.4\",\"-1200\":\"3.2\",\"-720\":\"3.2\",\"-240\":\"3.1\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Chloride\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(mEq/L)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":95,\"high\":105},\"-2160\":\"101\",\"-1680\":\"100\",\"-1200\":\"99\",\"-720\":\"98\",\"-240\":\"98\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"BUN\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(mg/dL)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":7,\"high\":20},\"-2160\":\"28\",\"-1680\":\"32\",\"-1200\":\"36\",\"-720\":\"37\",\"-240\":\"35\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Creatinine\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(mg/dL)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":0.6,\"high\":1.2},\"-2160\":\"1.3\",\"-1680\":\"1.4\",\"-1200\":\"1.5\",\"-720\":\"1.5\",\"-240\":\"1.4\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Glucose\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(mg/dL)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":70,\"high\":100},\"-2160\":\"142\",\"-1680\":\"156\",\"-1200\":\"168\",\"-720\":\"169\",\"-240\":\"172\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"CO2\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(mEq/L)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":23,\"high\":30},\"-2160\":\"23\",\"-1680\":\"22\",\"-1200\":\"21\",\"-720\":\"20\",\"-240\":\"20\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Calcium\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(mg/dL)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":8.5,\"high\":10.5},\"-2160\":\"8.7\",\"-1680\":\"8.6\",\"-1200\":\"8.6\",\"-720\":\"8.5\",\"-240\":\"8.5\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Lactate\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(mmol/L)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":0.5,\"high\":1},\"-2160\":\"\",\"-1680\":\"\",\"-1200\":\"\",\"-720\":\"\",\"-240\":\"\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"HbA1c\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"%\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":4,\"high\":5.6},\"-2160\":\"\",\"-1680\":\"\",\"-1200\":\"\",\"-720\":\"\",\"-240\":\"\"},{\"field\":\"Hematology\",\"rowType\":\"divider\",\"unit\":\"\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"RBC\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(10⁶/µL)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":4,\"high\":6},\"-2160\":\"\",\"-1680\":\"\",\"-1200\":\"\",\"-720\":\"\",\"-240\":\"\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Hemoglobin\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(g/dL)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":12,\"high\":17.5},\"-2160\":\"9.4\",\"-1680\":\"8.6\",\"-1200\":\"7.4\",\"-720\":\"7.2\",\"-240\":\"6.9\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Hematocrit\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(%)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":36,\"high\":54},\"-2160\":\"29\",\"-1680\":\"26\",\"-1200\":\"22\",\"-720\":\"21\",\"-240\":\"20\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"MCV\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(fL)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":80,\"high\":100},\"-2160\":\"\",\"-1680\":\"\",\"-1200\":\"\",\"-720\":\"\",\"-240\":\"\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"MCH\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(pg)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":27,\"high\":33},\"-2160\":\"\",\"-1680\":\"\",\"-1200\":\"\",\"-720\":\"\",\"-240\":\"\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"MCHC\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(g/dL)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":32,\"high\":36},\"-2160\":\"\",\"-1680\":\"\",\"-1200\":\"\",\"-720\":\"\",\"-240\":\"\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"WBC\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"(10³/µL)\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":4.5,\"high\":11},\"-2160\":\"8.4\",\"-1680\":\"9.2\",\"-1200\":\"10.1\",\"-720\":\"10.6\",\"-240\":\"11.3\"},{\"0\":\"\",\"field\":\"Neutrophils\",\"rowType\":\"results\",\"unit\":\"%\",\"normalRange\":{\"low\":55,\"high\":70},\"-2160\":\"\",\"-1680\":\"\",\"-120