c638b9ff5\",\"administratorId\":\"Sierra Johnson, RN\",\"adminTimeMinuteOffset\":-1920,\"status\":\"Given\",\"administeredDose\":20,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"id\":\"8c35bfbc-eea7-4711-a51b-2d32895995a2\",\"medicationOrderId\":\"a389e3b0-2f9a-475f-b4c9-517c638b9ff5\",\"administratorId\":\"Sierra Johnson, RN\",\"adminTimeMinuteOffset\":-1200,\"status\":\"Given\",\"administeredDose\":20,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"id\":\"8d9f9829-a335-4cbc-8665-f06e5b65529f\",\"medicationOrderId\":\"1f92e85c-2714-41ee-baa7-079fc1709580\",\"administratorId\":\"Tessa Ludwig, RN\",\"adminTimeMinuteOffset\":-2160,\"status\":\"Given\",\"administeredDose\":1000,\"visibleInPresim\":true}]}"', 'Case Thomas Dunn', '2026-06-17 18:45:20.208743+00', '2026-06-17 18:45:20.208743+00'),
	('150e5e97-f850-4589-bce6-6d2b2445149e', '"{\"demographics\":{\"DOBDay\":\"15\",\"DOBMonth\":\"March\",\"admissionDateOffest\":\"0\",\"admissionTime\":\"09:34\",\"admittingDiagnosis\":\"Chest Pain\",\"age\":\"56\",\"attendingProviderName\":\"Sarah Patel\",\"attendingProviderTitle\":\"MD\",\"codeStatus\":\"Full\",\"dosingWeight\":\"88\",\"employment\":\"Secretary\",\"firstName\":\"Susan\",\"heightFeet\":\"5\",\"heightInches\":\"6\",\"insurance\":\"Private\",\"language\":\"English\",\"needsInterpreter\":false,\"lastName\":\"Dickson\",\"precautions\":\"None\",\"relationshipStatus\":\"Married\",\"religion\":\"NA\",\"summary\":\"Susan Dickson is a 56-year-old female who arrived at the Emergency Department (ED) with acute chest pain. Her initial diagnostic data—labs and EKG—are inconclusive for myocardial infarction (MI), requiring further assessment and monitoring.\",\"contact\":\"Anthony Dickson\",\"contactRelationship\":\"Husband\",\"contactPhone\":\"(555) 210-8976\"},\"history\":{\"medicalHistory\":[\"HTN\",\"GERD\",\"HLD\"],\"surgicalHistory\":[],\"familyHistory\":[{\"relation\":\"Father\",\"condition\":\"MI at 60- deceased\"},{\"relation\":\"Mother\",\"condition\":\"HTN, breast cancer\"}],\"socialHistory\":[\"Former-smoker\",\"Social drinker, 1-2 drinks/week\"],\"livingSituation\":[\"Lives with husband in single-story home\"],\"allergies\":[\"Penicillin\"],\"alerts\":[\"NPO Status\",\"High Risk for Falls - Morse score > 45\"]},\"notes\":[{\"title\":\"Consult Note\",\"author\":\"Dr. Reynolds\",\"specialty\":\"Cardiology\",\"timeOffset\":-240,\"content\":\"<p>CARDIOLOGY CONSULT NOTE</p><p><strong>Consult History:</strong></p><p>Patient evaluated in emergency department at request of emergency medicine provider for persistent chest pain concerning for possible cardiac etiology.</p><p>Patient reports onset of midsternal chest pressure earlier today while at home. Pain described as pressure-like sensation with radiation into upper back. Initial pain severity reported at 7/10, currently improved to 4/10 after administration of sublingual nitroglycerin.</p><p>Associated symptoms include mild nausea and indigestion sensation. Patient denies dyspnea, diaphoresis, syncope, or palpitations.</p><p>Significant cardiac risk factors include hypertension, hyperlipidemia, former heavy smoking history, and family history of coronary artery disease.</p><p><strong>Cardiac Review:</strong></p><p>ECG reviewed. Sinus rhythm present without ST elevation. Mild non-specific T wave abnormality noted in inferior leads.</p><p>Initial troponin I reviewed at 0.03 ng/mL, borderline but non-diagnostic.</p><p>Patient remains hemodynamically stable at time of evaluation.</p><p><strong>Assessment:</strong></p><p>Chest pain concerning for possible unstable angina versus evolving non-ST elevation myocardial infarction.</p><p>Current workup remains inconclusive, however patient has several significant cardiovascular risk factors requiring continued cardiac monitoring and serial biomarker evaluation.</p><p>Low suspicion for STEMI at present.</p><p><strong>Recommendations:</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Continue telemetry monitoring</p></li><li><p>Trend troponin q3 hours</p></li><li><p>Repeat 12-lead ECG with recurrent chest pain or clinical change</p></li><li><p>Continue aspirin therapy</p></li><li><p>Nitroglycerin PRN chest discomfort</p></li><li><p>Consider initiation of beta blocker therapy if blood pressure remains elevated</p></li><li><p>Maintain NPO status pending possible stress testing versus cardiac catheterization if troponin elevates</p></li><li><p>Cardiology to continue following</p></li></ul><p><strong>Impression:</strong></p><ol class=\\\"list-decimal ml-10\\\"><li><p>Chest Pain suspicious for Acute Coronary Syndrome</p></li><li><p>Rule Out NSTEMI</p></li><li><p>Possible unstable angina</p></li><li><p>Multiple cardiac risk factors present</p></li></ol><p></p><p>Electronically Signed<br>Michael Reynolds, MD<br>Cardiology</p>\",\"excludedFromPresim\":false},{\"title\":\"History & Physical Note\",\"author\":\"Dr. Samuel Johnson\",\"specialty\":\"Emergency Medicine\",\"timeOffset\":-270,\"content\":\"<p><strong>Chief Complaint:</strong> Chest pain</p><p>Ms. Dickson is an adult female presenting to the emergency department with complaints of persistent substernal chest pressure that began several hours prior to arrival while at home performing normal daily activities. Patient describes discomfort as a pressure sensation located mid-sternum with radiation to the upper back. Pain initially rated 7/10 and has remained persistent despite rest.</p><p>Patient reports associated mild nausea and indigestion sensation. Denies shortness of breath, diaphoresis, dizziness, syncope, palpitations, fever, recent illness, cough, or lower extremity swelling.</p><p>Given persistent symptoms and concern for possible cardiac etiology, patient presented to ED for evaluation.</p><p>Past medical history: HTN, HLD, GERD</p><p>Home medications: </p><p>-Lisinopril 10mg BID</p><p>-Omeprazole 20mg daily</p><p>-Atorvastatin 20mg daily</p><p>Patient states she took all home medications this morning prior to arrival to ED.</p><p>Family history: Father died from MI at age 60, mother HTN and breast CA</p><p>Social history: former smoker, quit 2 years ago (2packs/day), social alcohol use, denies recreational drug use</p><p><strong>Vital Signs:</strong></p><p>BP: 148/92 mmHg</p><p>HR: 96 bpm</p><p>RR: 20/min</p><p>Temp: 98.4F</p><p>SpO2: 96% room air</p><p><strong>Physical Exam:</strong></p><p>General: Alert, oriented x4, mildly uncomfortable secondary to chest pain.</p><p>Cardiac: Regular rate and rhythm. No murmurs appreciated. Peripheral pulses intact.</p><p>Respiratory: Lungs clear bilaterally. No respiratory distress.</p><p>GI: Abdomen soft, non-tender, non-distended.</p><p>Skin: Warm, dry, no diaphoresis.</p><p>Neurologic: No focal deficits noted.</p><p><strong>Diagnostic Results</strong>:</p><p>12-Lead ECG:<br>Normal sinus rhythm. No ST elevation. Non-specific T wave inversion noted in lead III. No STEMI criteria met.</p><p>Initial Troponin I: 0.03 ng/mL<br>(Lab cutoff 0.04 ng/mL)</p><p>BMP/CMP: Within normal limits</p><p>Chest X-Ray: No acute cardiopulmonary abnormalities</p><p><strong>ED Interventions:</strong></p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Cardiac monitor initiated</p></li><li><p>Peripheral IV established</p></li><li><p>Aspirin 325 mg PO administered</p></li><li><p>Nitroglycerin 0.4 mg SL x1 administered</p></li><li><p>Morphine 2mg IV once</p></li><li><p>Cardiology consulted due to persistent chest pain with abnormal ECG findings</p></li></ul><p>Differential includes:</p><p>-Acute Coronary Syndrome / NSTEMI</p><p>-Unstable Angina</p><p>-GERD exacerbation</p><p>-Esophageal spasm</p><p>-Musculoskeletal chest pain</p><p><strong>Plan:</strong></p><p>Admit to telemetry observation.</p><p>Orders placed for:</p><ul class=\\\"list-disc ml-6\\\"><li><p>Continuous telemetry monitoring</p></li><li><p>Nitroglycerin PRN chest pain</p></li><li><p>Metoprolol tartrate 25 mg PO PRN SBP &gt;160</p></li><li><p>Cardiology consultation</p></li><li><p>NPO pending further workup</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Electronically Signed<br>Samuel Johnson, MD<br>Emergency Medicine</p>\",\"excludedFromPresim\":false}],\"orders\":[{\"category\":\"Laboratory\",\"title\":\"Basic Metabolic Panel (BMP)\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"details\":\"Collect Basic Metabolic Panel (BMP).\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Laboratory\",\"title\":\"Complete Blood Count (CBC)\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"details\":\"Collect Complete Blood Count (CBC).\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"important\":false,\"category\":\"Respiratory\",\"title\":\"Oxygen Therapy\",\"details\":\"Administer oxygen via nasal cannula at 2 L/min. Titrate to maintain SpO₂ ≥ 92%.\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Azzedine Habz\",\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Insert and Maintain IV\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"details\":\"\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"important\":false,\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Fall Risk Precautions\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"details\":\"Implement standard fall risk protocol. Ensure bed in low position and call light within reach.\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. John Smith, MD\",\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Activity: Bedrest\",\"details\":\"Bedrest with bathroom privileges until further cardiac workup. \",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Johnson\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Vital Signs Monitoring (q2h)\",\"details\":\"Monitor BP, HR, RR, Temp, SpO₂ every 2 hours. Notify provider for Temp > 38.0°C (100.4°F), Systolic BP > 160 mmHg or < 100 mmHg, HR > 110 bpm or < 50 bpm.\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Johnson\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Diet\",\"title\":\"NPO\",\"details\":\"Nothing by mouth except medications\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Johnson\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"ECG q3h\",\"details\":\"Repeat ECG q3h or with increase in chest pain/worsening patient condition. Notify provider when completed.\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Johnson\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Laboratory\",\"title\":\"Troponin\",\"details\":\"Repeat troponin q3h\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Johnson\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true},{\"category\":\"Nursing\",\"title\":\"Telemetry\",\"details\":\"Continuous cardiac monitoring: acute chest pain\",\"status\":\"Active\",\"orderingProvider\":\"Dr. Johnson\",\"important\":true,\"visibleInPresim\":true}],\"labs\":{\